Project Overview: This project aims to assemble, annotat, and compare the genomes of two sexually reproducing whiptail lizards, Aspidoscelis gularis and Aspidoscelis sexlineatus. I plan to compare genomic characteristics and gene organization between the two species using synteny analysis.

Pipeline:
1. Meryl – Count k-mers from sequencing reads.
2. GenomeScope 2.0 – Estimate genome size, heterozygosity, and repetitive sequence content.
3. hifiasm – Assemble genomes from PacBio HiFi reads.
4. SeqKit – Calculate genome assembly statistics.
5.Kraken2 – Screen assemblies for potential contamination.
6. BUSCO – Evaluate genome completeness.
7. Earl Grey – Identify and annotate repetitive elements.
8. Tiberius – Predict protein-coding genes.
9. GENESPACE – Compare gene organization and identify conserved genomic regions.

Repository Contents:
README.md - project overview
ai_usage.md - documenation of AI use
scripts/ - commands and scripts used for analyses

